ation, and sshd reloads directly supported the task. The two reboots and their transient systemd units were required by the provider-wide restart protocol. Temporary files were trap-cleaned, and final snapshots show no failed services, damaged package state, unexpected listeners, or abandoned task files. Both restart protocols were complete: each node had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/configuration/data state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8108ba1b3cca4f93","cmd-b59bf43865c04567","cmd-249e915d581f4063","cmd-24504351f2954c06","cmd-9550ec26cea045fc","cmd-5385f6dfb0904ad2","cmd-c7e5ad377c7442c7","cmd-10022484b2524333","cmd-9c819bd8534c4b97","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. opsbot has persistent key-based command access from node1 to node2, key-only policy applies to opsbot on both systems, and the original RHEL release and kernel were preserved. Provider-wide restart evidence is complete and coherent for both nodes.","limitations":["No inbound SSH login was behaviorally exercised against node1; its key-only result is established through effective sshd policy inspection before and after restart.","Some later password-status and passwordauthentication fields were redacted or malformed in captured output. Earlier unredacted effective-policy checks, AuthenticationMethods publickey, locked-password evidence, and node2's negative authentication test compensate for this."]}
